<title>USA: Imark Technologies Q3 net loss up 95 pct.</title>
<headline>Imark Technologies Q3 net loss up 95 pct.</headline>
<dateline>RESTON, Va. 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Q3 results, period ended March 31</p>
<p>				1997			1996</p>
<p> Shr loss		   $0.13     loss	 $0.15</p>
<p> Net loss		 602,158     loss     308,401</p>
<p> Revs			 9,500			nil</p>
<p> Avg shrs	     4,781,270		2,047,300</p>
<p>	    9 MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr loss		   $0.41     loss	 $0.54</p>
<p> Net loss	     1,738,273     loss   1,037,122</p>
<p> Revs			37,004		    8,500</p>
<p> Avg shrs	     4,252,726		1,923,354</p>
<p>Notes: Imark Technologies Inc, formerly CD-Max Inc, said Q3 general and administrative costs rose to $255,807 from $37,259 a year ago due to the addition of staff and increased marketing efforts. Company plans to approach profitability in fiscal 1998, it said. The name change from CD-Max to Imark was announced last month. Shareholder approval is pending. Stock is still trading under.</p>
</text>
